"text": "Slide out the tray and cut a small window in its center. Then cut a smaller hole in the outer sleeve, color the insides black, and tape a square of soda can over the hole. Poke a tiny pinhole through the aluminum and cover it with tape to make a shutter. In complete darkness, run 35mm film through the box and tape its end to an empty film canister. Slide the tray back in, seal every gap with electrical tape, and add a ring to help wind the film. Point it at your subjects, uncover the pinhole for a few seconds, cover it again, then wind the film forward. And once developed, you'll have a photograph.",
